{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/martinring/tmlanguage/master/tmlanguage.json",
  "name": "Rux",
  "scopeName": "source.rux",
  "fileTypes": [
    "rux"
  ],
  "patterns": [
    {
      "include": "#section-template"
    },
    {
      "include": "#section-style"
    },
    {
      "include": "#section-script"
    }
  ],
  "repository": {
    "section-template": {
      "comment": "Tolerant of attributes for the reason given on `section-style`, even though `<template>` takes none today. An unmatched section costs the file its highlighting.",
      "begin": "(<)(template)((?:\\s+[^<>]*?)?)\\s*(>)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.begin.rux"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.tag.section.rux"
        },
        "3": {
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#tag-attributes"
            }
          ]
        },
        "4": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.end.rux"
        }
      },
      "end": "(</)(template)\\s*(>)",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.begin.rux"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.tag.section.rux"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.end.rux"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#template-content"
        }
      ]
    },
    "section-style": {
      "comment": "The attribute group is not decoration: `<style src=\"theme.css\">` is how an external stylesheet is included, and a begin pattern demanding `>` straight after the name failed to match it. The top level of this grammar is only the three sections, so a section that does not match leaves its whole contents unscoped and the file looks unhighlighted.",
      "begin": "(<)(style)((?:\\s+[^<>]*?)?)\\s*(>)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.begin.rux"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.tag.section.rux"
        },
        "3": {
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#tag-attributes"
            }
          ]
        },
        "4": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.end.rux"
        }
      },
      "end": "(</)(style)\\s*(>)",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.begin.rux"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.tag.section.rux"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.end.rux"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#css"
        }
      ]
    },
    "section-script": {
      "comment": "Tolerant of attributes for the reason given on `section-style`.",
      "begin": "(<)(script)((?:\\s+[^<>]*?)?)\\s*(>)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.begin.rux"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.tag.section.rux"
        },
        "3": {
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#tag-attributes"
            }
          ]
        },
        "4": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.end.rux"
        }
      },
      "end": "(</)(script)\\s*(>)",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.begin.rux"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.tag.section.rux"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.end.rux"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#script-body"
        }
      ]
    },
    "template-content": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#html-comment"
        },
        {
          "include": "#interpolation"
        },
        {
          "include": "#tag-element"
        },
        {
          "include": "#tag"
        }
      ]
    },
    "html-comment": {
      "name": "comment.block.html.rux",
      "begin": "<!--",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "0": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.comment.rux"
        }
      },
      "end": "-->",
      "endCaptures": {
        "0": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.comment.rux"
        }
      }
    },
    "interpolation": {
      "name": "meta.interpolation.rux",
      "begin": "\\{\\{",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "0": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.interpolation.begin.rux"
        }
      },
      "end": "\\}\\}",
      "endCaptures": {
        "0": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.interpolation.end.rux"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "meta.embedded.expression.rux",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#script-expression"
        }
      ]
    },
    "tag": {
      "begin": "(</?)([a-zA-Z][\\w.-]*)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.begin.rux"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "support.class.component.rux"
        }
      },
      "end": "(/?>)",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.end.rux"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#tag-attributes"
        }
      ],
      "comment": "Any tag the element rule above did not claim, which by construction is a component: Rux's elements are a closed set, so a name outside it is somebody's file. Two rules rather than one alternation with two capture groups, because the highlighter scoped only the second branch of that and left every element uncoloured. The scope is `support.class`, not an `entity.name.tag.*` refinement, and that is the whole point: a TextMate scope inherits every theme rule written for its prefixes, so `entity.name.tag.component.rux` took the plain tag colour in every stock theme and the distinction existed only in the grammar file. `support.class` is what Vue and Svelte scope a component tag to, and themes colour it apart from a tag."
    },
    "tag-attributes": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#directive-attribute"
        },
        {
          "include": "#plain-attribute"
        }
      ]
    },
    "directive-attribute": {
      "comment": "r-for / r-if / r-model, @event handlers, :prop bindings, and a route `guard`. The value is a Rux script expression in every case.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "begin": "(@[\\w-]+|:[\\w-]+|r-[\\w-]+|guard)(=)(\")",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "entity.other.attribute-name.directive.rux"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "punctuation.separator.key-value.rux"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.rux"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\")",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.rux"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.expression.rux",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#script-expression"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "begin": "(@[\\w-]+|:[\\w-]+|r-[\\w-]+|guard)(=)(')",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "entity.other.attribute-name.directive.rux"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "punctuation.separator.key-value.rux"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.rux"
            }
          },
          "end": "(')",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.rux"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.expression.rux",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#script-expression"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "plain-attribute": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "match": "\\b([a-zA-Z][\\w-]*)(?=\\s*=)",
          "name": "entity.other.attribute-name.rux"
        },
        {
          "match": "\\b([a-zA-Z][\\w-]*)\\b",
          "name": "entity.other.attribute-name.rux"
        },
        {
          "name": "string.quoted.double.rux",
          "begin": "\"",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "0": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.rux"
            }
          },
          "end": "\"",
          "endCaptures": {
            "0": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.rux"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "string.quoted.single.rux",
          "begin": "'",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "0": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.rux"
            }
          },
          "end": "'",
          "endCaptures": {
            "0": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.rux"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "css": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#css-comment"
        },
        {
          "include": "#css-at-rule"
        },
        {
          "include": "#css-selector"
        },
        {
          "include": "#css-block"
        }
      ]
    },
    "css-block": {
      "begin": "\\{",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "0": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.property-list.begin.css.rux"
        }
      },
      "end": "\\}",
      "endCaptures": {
        "0": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.property-list.end.css.rux"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#css-comment"
        },
        {
          "include": "#css-declaration"
        },
        {
          "include": "#css-selector"
        },
        {
          "include": "#css-block"
        }
      ]
    },
    "css-comment": {
      "name": "comment.block.css.rux",
      "begin": "/\\*",
      "end": "\\*/"
    },
    "css-at-rule": {
      "match": "(@)([a-zA-Z-]+)",
      "name": "keyword.control.at-rule.css.rux"
    },
    "css-selector": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "match": "\\.[a-zA-Z_][\\w-]*",
          "name": "entity.other.attribute-name.class.css.rux"
        },
        {
          "match": "#[a-zA-Z_][\\w-]*",
          "name": "entity.other.attribute-name.id.css.rux"
        },
        {
          "match": "(::?)([a-zA-Z-]+)",
          "name": "entity.other.attribute-name.pseudo-class.css.rux"
        },
        {
          "match": "[>+~]",
          "name": "keyword.operator.combinator.css.rux"
        }
      ]
    },
    "css-declaration": {
      "begin": "([a-zA-Z-]+)(\\s*)(:)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "support.type.property-name.css.rux"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "punctuation.separator.key-value.css.rux"
        }
      },
      "end": "(;)|(?=\\})",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.terminator.rule.css.rux"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#css-value"
        }
      ]
    },
    "css-value": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#css-comment"
        },
        {
          "match": "#[0-9a-fA-F]{3,8}\\b",
          "name": "constant.other.color.rgb-value.css.rux"
        },
        {
          "match": "\\b([a-zA-Z-]+)(?=\\()",
          "name": "support.function.css.rux"
        },
        {
          "match": "!important\\b",
          "name": "keyword.other.important.css.rux"
        },
        {
          "match": "(-?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)(px|em|rem|%|vh|vw|vmin|vmax|deg|turn|rad|fr|s|ms|pt)?\\b",
          "name": "constant.numeric.css.rux"
        },
        {
          "name": "string.quoted.double.css.rux",
          "begin": "\"",
          "end": "\""
        },
        {
          "name": "string.quoted.single.css.rux",
          "begin": "'",
          "end": "'"
        },
        {
          "match": "\\b(solid|dashed|dotted|none|auto|flex|grid|block|inline|row|column|dense|center|start|end|flex-start|flex-end|space-between|space-around|stretch|wrap|nowrap|wrap-reverse|pointer|default|static|relative|sticky|absolute|fixed|hidden|clip|visible|scroll|bold|lighter|bolder|normal|italic|oblique|pre|underline|line-through|justify|left|right|break-word|break-all|anywhere|content|initial|cover|contain|transparent|linear|ease|ease-in|ease-out|ease-in-out|nonzero|evenodd|butt|round|square|miter|bevel)\\b",
          "name": "support.constant.property-value.css.rux"
        }
      ]
    },
    "script-body": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#script-comment"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-declaration"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-storage"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-use-path"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-keyword"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-boolean"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-lifecycle"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-signal"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-string"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-number"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-function-call"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-operator"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-identifier"
        }
      ]
    },
    "script-use-path": {
      "comment": "The path in `use components::header;`. Coloured apart from an ordinary identifier because it names a FILE (components/header.rux) and, from that, a tag (<header>). Listed before #script-keyword so it claims the `use` first and can colour the path with it.",
      "match": "\\b(use)\\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(?:::[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)*)",
      "captures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "keyword.control.import.rux"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.namespace.rux"
        }
      }
    },
    "script-expression": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#script-comment"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-declaration"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-keyword"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-boolean"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-lifecycle"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-signal"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-string"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-number"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-function-call"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-operator"
        },
        {
          "include": "#script-identifier"
        }
      ]
    },
    "script-comment": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "comment.line.double-slash.rux",
          "begin": "//",
          "end": "$"
        },
        {
          "name": "comment.block.rux",
          "begin": "/\\*",
          "end": "\\*/"
        }
      ]
    },
    "script-string": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "string.quoted.double.rux",
          "begin": "\"",
          "end": "\"",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "match": "\\\\.",
              "name": "constant.character.escape.rux"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "string.quoted.single.rux",
          "begin": "'",
          "end": "'",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "match": "\\\\.",
              "name": "constant.character.escape.rux"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "comment": "A backtick template literal. The whole run is a string, and the `${…}` holes inside it are code: without this the literal text and the interpolated expression were coloured identically, so `${search_item} I don't` gave no clue which half was a value.",
          "name": "string.template.rux",
          "begin": "`",
          "end": "`",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "0": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.rux"
            }
          },
          "endCaptures": {
            "0": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.rux"
            }
          },
          "patterns": [
            {
              "match": "\\\\.",
              "name": "constant.character.escape.rux"
            },
            {
              "name": "meta.template.expression.rux",
              "begin": "\\$\\{",
              "end": "\\}",
              "beginCaptures": {
                "0": {
                  "name": "punctuation.definition.template-expression.begin.rux"
                }
              },
              "endCaptures": {
                "0": {
                  "name": "punctuation.definition.template-expression.end.rux"
                }
              },
              "contentName": "meta.embedded.line.rux",
              "patterns": [
                {
                  "include": "#script-boolean"
                },
                {
                  "include": "#script-signal"
                },
                {
                  "include": "#script-string"
                },
                {
                  "include": "#script-number"
                },
                {
                  "include": "#script-function-call"
                },
                {
                  "include": "#script-operator"
                },
                {
                  "include": "#script-identifier"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "script-number": {
      "match": "\\b(-?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\b",
      "name": "constant.numeric.rux"
    },
    "script-boolean": {
      "match": "\\b(true|false)\\b",
      "name": "constant.language.rux"
    },
    "script-keyword": {
      "comment": "`use` is Rux's import statement and was missing, so it rendered as plain text next to a coloured `let` on the following line. `import` is rhai's word for it; Rux does not use it, but it costs nothing to colour.",
      "match": "\\b(use|if|else|for|in|while|loop|return|break|continue|switch|throw|try|catch|import|as|private)\\b",
      "name": "keyword.control.rux"
    },
    "script-storage": {
      "match": "\\b(let|const|fn)\\b",
      "name": "storage.type.rux"
    },
    "script-lifecycle": {
      "comment": "`mounted { … }`, `unmounted { … }` and `effect { … }` are blocks rather than calls, so #script-signal's lookahead for `(` never reaches them.",
      "match": "\\b(mounted|unmounted|effect)\\b(?=\\s*\\{)",
      "name": "support.function.builtin.rux"
    },
    "script-signal": {
      "comment": "`computed` and `effect` are NOT here on purpose. This rule ends in a `(?=\\s*\\()` lookahead, so it only ever matches a call; `computed name = expr;` is a declaration and `effect { … }` is a block, and both went uncoloured for as long as they were listed here. They live in #script-declaration and #script-lifecycle now.",
      "match": "\\b(signal|query|navigate|replace|back|forward|path_for|emit|print|debug|blur|setInterval|clearInterval)\\b(?=\\s*\\()",
      "name": "support.function.builtin.rux"
    },
    "script-function-call": {
      "match": "\\b([a-zA-Z_]\\w*)\\s*(?=\\()",
      "name": "entity.name.function.rux"
    },
    "script-operator": {
      "match": "(==|!=|<=|>=|&&|\\|\\||[-+*/%=<>!])",
      "name": "keyword.operator.rux"
    },
    "script-declaration": {
      "comment": "The declared name gets a scope of its own so a variable is identifiable by sight. `computed` is a keyword here rather than a function, which is the whole difference between what the language has and what it looked like it had.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "comment": "`computed name = expr;` — a declaration, not a call.",
          "match": "\\b(computed)\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "storage.type.rux"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "variable.other.declaration.rux"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "comment": "`fn name(a, b)` — the name is the function being defined.",
          "match": "\\b(fn)\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "storage.type.function.rux"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "entity.name.function.rux"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "match": "\\b(let|const)\\s+([A-Za-z_]\\w*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "storage.type.rux"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "variable.other.declaration.rux"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "script-identifier": {
      "comment": "A bare name, so a variable reference is identifiable by sight and not only where it is declared. This must be LAST in any pattern list: every more specific rule (keyword, builtin, function call) is tried first and only what is left over is a plain variable. Inside a `${…}` hole it is what stops the expression inheriting the enclosing string colour, which made the interpolated value and the literal text look identical.",
      "match": "\\b[A-Za-z_]\\w*\\b",
      "name": "variable.other.rux"
    },
    "tag-element": {
      "begin": "(</?)(screen|view|text|image|path|button|input|slot|router|route)(?![\\w.-])",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.begin.rux"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.tag.rux"
        }
      },
      "end": "(/?>)",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.tag.end.rux"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#tag-attributes"
        }
      ],
      "comment": "Rux's ten elements, matched whole so `views` is not `view`. Everything else falls through to #tag and is coloured as a component, which is the single most useful distinction in a template: markup you can look up in the reference, against markup you have to go and open."
    }
  }
}
